<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!--
Alabama Appellate Courts - Case Detail API Response
====================================================

This XSD documents the JSON API response structure from the Alabama
appellate courts case detail endpoint.

API Endpoint:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}

URL Parameters:
- court-guid: Court GUID (e.g., "68f021c4-6a44-4735-9a76-5360b2e8af13")
- case-uuid: Case instance UUID

Response Format: JSON

The response contains complete case metadata including header information,
originating court details, and case status.

Example Response Structure:
{
    "caseHeader": {
        "caseInstanceUUID": "abc123...",
        "caseNumber": "SC-2023-0123",
        "caseTitle": "Ex parte State",
        "caseCaption": "Ex parte State of Alabama",
        "courtID": 68,
        "courtAbbreviation": "Alabama Supreme Court",
        "filedDate": "2023-11-09T14:15:00.000+00:00",
        "caseClassification": "Appeal - Civil - Other",
        "closedFlag": false,
        "originatingCourtCases": [
            {
                "originatingCourtName": "Mobile Circuit Court",
                "originatingCaseNumber": "CC-2022-901234"
            }
        ]
    }
}

Case Header Fields:
- caseInstanceUUID: Unique identifier for the case
- caseNumber: Official case number (e.g., "SC-2023-0123")
- caseTitle: Short case title
- caseCaption: Full formal case caption (preferred for case_name)
- courtID: Numeric court identifier (68=Supreme, 69=Civil, 70=Criminal)
- filedDate: Date the case was filed (ISO 8601)
- caseClassification: Case type/classification
- closedFlag: Boolean indicating if the case is closed

Originating Court Information:
- originatingCourtCases[]: Array of lower court cases (usually one)
  - originatingCourtName: Name of the lower court
  - originatingCaseNumber: Lower court case number
- Multiple originating cases possible for consolidated appeals

Data Extraction:
- case_name: Use caseCaption if available, otherwise caseTitle
- date_filed: Extracted from filedDate (ISO 8601 format)
- originating_court: From originatingCourtCases[0].originatingCourtName
- originating_court_number: From originatingCourtCases[0].originatingCaseNumber
- status: "Closed" if closedFlag is true, otherwise "Open"
- court_id: Mapped from courtID using _get_court_id_from_guid()

Source URL Pattern:
https://publicportal.alappeals.gov/portal/court/{court-guid}/case/{case-uuid}

Next Steps:
After parsing case detail, the scraper fetches:
1. Parties: https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}/parties
2. Docket Entries: https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}/docketentries

-->

<xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
        This is a documentation-only XSD for the Alabama Case Detail API.
        The actual response is JSON, not XML.
    </xs:documentation>
</xs:annotation>

</xs:schema>
